From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: accept non-WMT frames at full-STP TX init

The second Bluetooth H1 boot got its BT function-on event, then failed
to prepare HCI Reset with -EINVAL before any byte was sent. The TX
initializer validated the encoded frame with the WMT-only decoder, which
refuses every task other than WMT, so no task-0 command could be sent.

Validate with the shared full-STP decoder and keep the WMT command size
limit. The caller still selects and checks the task.

Unsigned experiment draft; archive identity is non-certifying.
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/wmt-full-stp-tx.h | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/wmt-full-stp-tx.h b/drivers/soc/mediatek/wmt-full-stp-tx.h
index e41258abf..f7248a2cd 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/wmt-full-stp-tx.h
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/wmt-full-stp-tx.h
@@ -14,13 +14,15 @@ struct wmt_full_tx {
 	int retired;
 };
 
+/* Any ordinary-task full-STP frame or ACK; the caller selects the task. */
 static inline int wmt_full_tx_init(struct wmt_full_tx *tx,
 				   const unsigned char *frame, unsigned int length)
 {
-	struct wmt_full_frame decoded;
+	struct stp_full_frame decoded;
 	struct wmt_full_tx initial = { .frame = frame, .length = length };
 
-	if (!tx || wmt_full_decode(frame, length, &decoded) < 0)
+	if (!tx || stp_full_decode(frame, length, &decoded) < 0 ||
+	    decoded.length > WMT_FULL_MAX_PAYLOAD)
 		return -1;
 	*tx = initial;
 	return 0;
